            "body": "All right. I've gone too many times back and fourth with it. In the end, I think it is best to not be part of 'mini.misc', but in the eventual 'mini.cmdline'.\r\n\r\nWith the introduction of the `vim._extui` in Neovim=0.12 (that will handle how command line is visualized), the 'mini.cmdline' scope is significantly reduced and I am currently looking into non-trivial enhancements of command line experience. Currently I have #690 and #1605 (both are out of scope for `vim._extui`, I asked). Which is not nothing, but I'd like to search a bit more for suggestions.\r\n\r\nSo all in all, I think I am going to close this in favor of a (more general) solution in 'mini.cmdline'. Thanks for your time and efforts, though :pray:",
